    keyword: `Corporate Card`,
    slug: `corporate-card`,
    sheet: `C`,
    definition: `<p>A corporate card is a business-issued payment card used by employees to pay for authorised work-related expenses such as travel, meals, fuel, subscriptions, utilities, and operational purchases. It centralises company spending, improves visibility, and simplifies tracking and reconciliation for finance teams.</p>`,
    sectionHeading1: `What Is a Corporate Card`,
    sectionDescription1: `<p>A corporate card is a business-issued payment card used by employees to pay for authorised work-related expenses such as travel, meals, fuel, subscriptions, utilities, and operational purchases. It centralises company spending, improves visibility, and simplifies tracking and reconciliation for finance teams.</p>`,
    sectionHeading2: `Business Context`,
    sectionDescription2: `<p>Corporate cards help organisations manage employee and departmental spending more efficiently. Instead of out-of-pocket payments and manual reimbursements, cards provide:</p><p>1. Controlled access to company funds</p><p>2. Real-time transaction visibility</p><p>3. Clear audit trails</p><p>4. Category-level restrictions</p><p>5. Easier reconciliations for month-end close</p><p>They are widely used across finance, sales, operations, procurement, admin, and field teams.</p>`,
    sectionHeading3: `How Corporate Cards Work`,
    sectionDescription3: `<p>Employees receive cards with predefined limits, categories, and policies set by the finance team. When used for business expenses:</p><p>i. Transactions are logged instantly</p><p>ii. Controls block unauthorised spending</p><p>iii. Digital receipts can be attached</p><p>iv. Approvals follow a pre-set workflow</p><p>v. Expenses sync with accounting and ERP tools</p><p>Corporate cards can be prepaid, credit, or expense-only depending on company policy and regulatory framework.</p>`,
    sectionHeading4: `Types of Corporate Cards`,
    sectionDescription4: `<p>1. Prepaid Corporate Cards</p><p>Loaded with a predefined balance. Ideal for controlled spending.</p><p>2. Credit Corporate Cards</p><p>Issued with a credit line. Suitable for larger organisations with predictable spending habits.</p><p>3. Category-Specific Cards</p><p>Purpose-built cards such as:</p><p>i. Travel cards</p><p>ii. Meal cards</p><p>iii. Fuel cards</p><p>iv. Purchase cards</p><p>v. Marketing cards</p><p>4. Virtual Cards</p><p>Instant, one-time or multi-use digital cards for subscriptions, online vendor payments, and secure transactions.</p>`,
    sectionHeading5: `How EnKash Helps`,
    sectionDescription5: `<p>EnKash offers one of India’s most advanced corporate card infrastructures, purpose-built for complete control, compliance, and visibility.</p><p>From prepaid cards to virtual and category-specific cards, every spend is tracked in real time, governed by policy-level controls, and reconciled automatically.</p><p>Finance teams manage all company-wide spending from a single, intelligent platform designed to eliminate leakage, simplify audits, and accelerate month-end close.</p>`,
